@* Both are a real <select>. The difference is only which arrow you get: NativeSelect keeps the
   platform's own control in a shadcn frame, and Select replaces the arrow to match the rest of
   the system. Neither needs JavaScript, both post the same way, and both bring the OS picker on
   a phone — so this is a decision about how it looks and about nothing else. *@
<div class="flex w-[420px] flex-col gap-4">
    <Field>
        <FieldLabel For="cmp-native">NativeSelect</FieldLabel>
        <NativeSelect id="cmp-native" name="a">
            <option>The platform draws the arrow</option>
        </NativeSelect>
    </Field>
    <Field>
        <FieldLabel For="cmp-select">Select</FieldLabel>
        <Select id="cmp-select" name="b">
            <SelectItem Value="x">ui.behavior.css draws it</SelectItem>
        </Select>
    </Field>
</div>
